      "id": "def-stalk-of-presheaf",
      "location": "Definition",
      "defect": "ill-formed",
      "evidence": "The item defines the neighbourhood category as the full subcategory of Open(X), while def-open-set-category-topological-space says its arrows are \"V \\to U when V \\subseteq U\". It then calls \\(\\mathcal F_x=\\varinjlim_{x\\in U}\\mathcal F(U)\\) a filtered colimit. But def-presheaf-on-topological-space makes \\(\\mathcal F\\) contravariant, so its restriction is a diagram \\(\\mathcal N_x^{op}\\to\\mathbf{Set}\\), not a diagram on the displayed full subcategory \\(\\mathcal N_x\\). The cited filtered-colimit definition requires a diagram \\(D:\\mathcal J\\to\\mathbf{Set}\\). Thus the stated category does not type the asserted colimit; the index must be explicitly reversed.",
      "severity": "fatal",
      "observed_sha256": "2172ccb95af66ed42e1168394950fb6335ec815e9241f7dac260ed4baad69dec"
    },
    {
