      "location": "Proof step 3.1",
      "defect": "unlicensed-inference",
      "evidence": "Step 3.1 calls \\(\\{B_x:x\\in U_\\alpha\\}\\) \"the basis cover of \\(U_\\alpha\\)\", but step 1.2 only chose \\(B_x\\subseteq U_{\\alpha(x)}\\), not \\(B_x\\subseteq U_\\alpha\\). If \\(x\\in U_\\alpha\\cap U_\\beta\\) and \\(\\alpha(x)=\\beta\\), the selected \\(B_x\\) may extend outside \\(U_\\alpha\\). Hence this family need not be a cover by basis elements of \\(U_\\alpha\\), so the assumed basis condition cannot yet be applied. Refining by basis elements inside \\(B_x\\cap U_\\alpha\\) repairs the gap.",
      "severity": "nonfatal",
      "observed_sha256": "e590824cd49a8c3441e10e601afa89ca2891114403ab8ffd5d38d7b92fa46a87"
    },
    {
