      "defect": "overstrong-title-or-statement",
      "evidence": "The page says the germ examples show \"why one point never determines a section\". For the one-point space \\(X=\\{x\\}\\), the only open neighbourhood of \\(x\\) is \\(X\\), so for any sheaf \\(\\mathcal F\\) the stalk \\(\\mathcal F_x\\) is canonically \\(\\mathcal F(X)\\); the germ at \\(x\\) does determine the global section. The intended claim is only that one stalk does not determine a section in general.",
