      "evidence": "After obtaining \\(s_x=s'_x\\) for every \\(x\\), step 4.1 says \"and then [L1] gives \\(s=s'\\)\". But [L1], lem-morphisms-of-sheaves-determined-by-stalks, concerns equality of two morphisms of sheaves from equality of their stalk maps; \\(s,s'\\) are sections, not morphisms or stalk maps. Equality follows instead by choosing local neighbourhoods from the germ equalities and applying sheaf locality, so the written inference is unsupported but immediately repairable.",
